-- ============================================================
-- TEMPLATE 000084 — Stylist Studio lifecycle collapse: backfill
-- Pixie Girl Hub · JBS Praxis · V2.2 · §6.24 (Stylist Studio)
--
-- Substitute {{BUSINESS}} with the brand schema (pixiegirl / faitlynhair).
-- Applied to EXISTING brands by repair-business-schema.js. Idempotent — the
-- WHERE clause filters on retired statuses, so a re-run touches zero rows.
--
-- WHY: the styling job lifecycle used to require four separate manual clicks
-- after Ops received the wig (qc pass → ready_for_dispatch → handed_to_sales
-- → completed). Nobody clicked all four, so every finished job got stuck in
-- qc_passed or handed_to_sales — and the scorecard aggregate keys on
-- `status = 'completed'`, so real, shipped work showed as "0 completed" on
-- every stylist's card.
--
-- Going forward, QC pass sets status directly to 'completed' and creates the
-- Logistics delivery (see src/modules/service_jobs/service-jobs.service.js
-- recordQc). This migration backfills the historical rows that got stuck in
-- the intermediate states so those completions retroactively show up.
--
-- Backfill rules:
--   status ∈ (qc_passed, ready_for_dispatch, handed_to_sales) → 'completed'
--   completed_at ← first non-null of: handed_at, ready_at, qc_at, updated_at
--
-- The CHECK constraint on status is NOT tightened — historical rows still
-- exist with the retired values in the audit log, and a future rebuild that
-- re-applies old data should not fail. Application code no longer writes them.
-- ============================================================

UPDATE {{BUSINESS}}.service_jobs
   SET status       = 'completed',
       completed_at = COALESCE(completed_at, handed_at, ready_at, qc_at, updated_at),
       updated_at   = now()
 WHERE status IN ('qc_passed', 'ready_for_dispatch', 'handed_to_sales');

